<speech id="uk.org.publicwhip/westminhall/2018-05-22a.326.6" speakername="Nick Gibb" person_id="uk.org.publicwhip/person/10225" colnum="326" time="15:16:00" url="">
    <p pid="a326.6/1">What the NEU is doing with its school cuts campaign is misleading. It is taking the cost pressures that we have acknowledged and telling the public that those are funding cuts. I have been clear that no school has had a funding cut. School funding went up in real terms per pupil in the last Parliament, and that increase has been maintained in real terms. The NEU is talking about cost pressures that have had to be absorbed, not just by the school system but by other parts of the public sector and the private sector. The hon. Lady will know that once the national funding formula is fully implemented, funding in South Tyneside will increase by 4.5%, which is equal to £3.9 million more going into schools in that area.</p>
</speech>
<gidredirect oldgid="uk.org.publicwhip/westminhall/2018-05-22a.327.0" newgid="uk.org.publicwhip/westminhall/2018-05-22b.327.0" matchtype="perfectmatch"/>
<gidredirect oldgid="uk.org.publicwhip/westminhall/2018-05-22a.327.1" newgid="uk.org.publicwhip/westminhall/2018-05-22b.327.1" matchtype="perfectmatch"/>
